  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1037 PM MDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nUpper high will shift slightly eastward Monday over the southern \nPlains before shifting and broadening across the southern US Tuesday \nand even into Wednesday. PWs stay above average with values \ngenerally 1.2\" to 1.3\". Storm chances continue each of those days \nwith a focus over the area mountains then isolated to scattered \nstorms in the desert lowlands. Gusty outflow winds and moderate to \nheavy downpours will be the primary hazards. \n\nBy Thursday and Friday, the upper high rebuilds over the \nsouthwestern US. Still can expect the normal monsoonal thunderstorms \nfor Thursday but by Friday and Saturday, PW values drop to 0.9\"-\n1.0\". Can expect a downtrend in activity due to this. Both the EC \nand GFS are showing a passing upper trough Sunday and Monday which \ncould bring some cooler weather if this does occur.",
